  "question": {
    "text": "A certain metallic surface is illuminated by monochromatic radiation of wavelength $\\lambda$. The stopping potential for photoelectric current for this radiation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the same surface is illuminated with a radiation of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the stopping potential is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The threshold wavelength of this surface for photoelectric effect is___________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced><mtext>&#160;and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p>"
  }
